From d3b192eb30a948eb528cf6afb5883895a6cbe72d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Dev Auditor <audit@massbattle.local>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:55:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] phase2-audit: seam home for the combat roll hash +
 binary-search defender lookups (B-2, A-4)

B-2: the melee roll's Knuth multipliers (2654435761u / 40503u / 2685821657u)
were duplicated across the seam boundary -- StaggeredPhaseOffset holds the
golden-ratio multiplier in BattleMelee.cpp while CombatResolutionProcessor
re-typed all three inline. A future edit to one site would silently break
the T2.8 determinism argument while the golden still passes (it only pins
the seam). Fix: FMeleeMath::CombatRoll01 -- one home, identical formula and
inputs (entity index, serial, the pair's own roll count; A13 preserved);
the processor calls it. Same bits out, verified structurally.

A-4: the assign write-back scanned the whole Defenders array per seeker
three times (stat mirror, ring defender, pair target). The seam sorts
Defenders handle-wise for exactly this; its binary search was file-local.
Fix: FCombatSolver::FindDefender exposed (same function the pass itself
uses); the write-back binary-searches. Identical results, O(n) -> O(log n)
per seeker per scan.

MUST re-run the unit tier (T2.1 golden + T2.3 assign invariants) and the
T2.8 DeterminismTwoRun func test on the UE machine.
